  "caption": "Quinn's first golf trip in a year meant 36 holes in two days. On hole 14 the back said no, and Quinn briefly considered quitting golf.\n\nKay explained that golf back pain often comes from repeated twisting and side-bending under load, especially after a sudden jump in rounds following a break. You usually don't need to stop golf completely.\n\nWhat can help: improving hip rotation, training trunk rotation and anti-rotation control, a 10-minute progressive warm-up, building rounds gradually, and asking a golf pro about side-bend in your swing.\n\nGet it checked if there's pain or numbness down the leg, leg weakness, marked night pain, or sudden severe pain, especially in older golfers.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
